Z||000026||Will||05-14-2001||01:07 PM||||You guys are all barking up the wrong tree.<P>A guy's car <I>CAN'T</I> be sexy or comfortable, because then women would want to drive it.<P>Guys (in no particular order):<P>993 or earlier wide-body whale tail Porsche. Nothing says "<I>power</I>" like this body style. Massaged by <A HREF="http://www.protomotive.com" TARGET=_blank>Protomotive Engineering</A> to produce 600 HP, of course. 996's an Boxsters are too girly.<BR>Or a 959.<BR>Grand National (or Monte Carlo SS) No curves, intimidating as HELL, fast as all get out. I was behind a done-up Monte on the interstate the other day. He got on it a couple of time to pass other cars--DAMN it sounded sweet.<BR>El Camino SS<BR>ZR1 Corvette<BR>Cobra R   NO creature comforts and loads of all kinds of performance--a REAL guy's car!<P>Hummer?<BR>De Tomaso Pantera?<P>Italian supercars are usually non-gender-specific because they are sexy, ergo both men and women want to drive them.<P>Girls (this is probably not a very good list, as I don't think about this much):<P>VW Bug  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>VW Cabriolet<BR>Dodge Neon<BR>Civic Hatchback<BR>Acura Integra LS<BR>Fiero. Sorry guys, but that's the way it is. Guys tell me my '87 GT is a piece of junk. Girls say "It's so CUTE!"||||reg||1
