Z||000048||Slammed Fiero||05-16-2001||07:34 PM||||We had a 72 Pantera with a built 351 , Very nice car , very tempremental. The AC system was a cause of a lot of problems , the wiring was a nightmare. Basically we replaced everywire in the car and re engineered the AC system. But the driving position , the V8 sound ..Ohhh soo nice. There a good deal for an exotic supercar.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000049||Got2manyfieros||05-16-2001||09:37 PM||||I am a little dissapointed in the selection in this topic:<BR>I think my top 5 cars would be:<BR>(any car with an automatic is OUT)<P>5) 2000 Mustang Cobra "R"<BR>4) Buick GSX (remember those?)<BR>3) 1995+ porche 911 turbo<BR>2) 1970 BOSS 429 mustang...not too good for the street, but by far the most intimidating front end of all the muscle cars.<BR>1) An ERA Shelby Cobra kit car with a SOHC Ford 427...I think that combination would really put some hair on your ass.<P>I love my fieros, but the fiero did not make the list because I look at my fiero as a pacifier until I can afford something spectacular.||||reg||1
